<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persaeus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 306–<a href="/years/243-bce">243 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Persaeus of Citium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Persaeus of Citium was a Stoic philosopher, a pupil and housemate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-of-citium">Zeno of Citium</a>. Sent by Zeno to the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-ii-gonatas">Antigonus II Gonatas</a> at Pella, he became a royal adviser and was later placed in command of the Macedonian garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a>, where he died, or according to some accounts escaped, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aratus-of-sicyon">Aratus of Sicyon</a> captured the citadel in 243 BCE.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Antigonus Gonatas was a student and friend of the Stoic Zeno of Citium, whose pupil <b>Persaeus</b> lived at his court; the poet Aratus of Soli wrote his astronomical poem, the Phaenomena, there; and the historian Hieronymus of Cardia, who served three generations of the dynasty, wrote the history…</blockquote><a href="/empire/antigonid-kingdom-of-macedonia">Antigonid Kingdom of Macedonia · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Kition, in what is now <a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.93,33.63&amp;year=-266" aria-label="Kition on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5403 900 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Persaeus"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5853 1170h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5853 1170h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=34.93,33.63&amp;year=-266">What was here in 266 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
